@@ -30,3 +30,12 @@ merged document as a new value; neither argument is mutated. The algorithm is th
 whole; an object patch is merged member by member, a `null` member removing the target's member, and a
 target that is not an object being treated as `{}`. Arrays are replaced, not merged, so a merge patch cannot
 set a member to `null`. It never throws. Only own members are read, and `__proto__` is handled as plain data.
+
+## Creating a JSON Patch (RFC 6902)
+
+`createPatch(from, to)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, returns a JSON Patch (an array of `add`, `remove` and
+`replace` operations) that `applyPatch` turns from `from` into `to`; neither argument is mutated and the
+patch shares no structure with them. It describes only what changed: objects are compared member by member,
+and arrays by longest common subsequence, so an inserted or removed item is a single `add` or `remove`, and
+a moved item is a `remove` plus an `add`, without rewriting the items around it. Identical documents give an
+empty patch; values of different types, or a changed root scalar, are replaced whole.
